.hm-loop-*

# PLAN-worktree-cross-session-data-loss-defense ADR-007:
# sandbox fixtures regen-only — every version bump re-renders ~2400+ files,
# two parallel sessions both bumping = guaranteed stash conflict at finalize.
# Untracking the currently-committed content via `git rm --cached` is a
# destructive operation requiring user authorization (see Phase 6 follow-up
# task). These .gitignore entries take effect AFTER `git rm --cached` runs.
tests/e2e/sandbox/
tests/e2e/sandbox-plugin-test/
tests/fixtures/*/CLAUDE.md
.claude/loop-specs/
work-docs/loop-context/

# ephemeral probe dirs written by tests/integration/test_env_isolation.py (cleaned in a
# finally block, and swept at import time; ignored here so a leftover is not git dirt.
# NOTE: gitignore cannot hide it from the run-time directory gate — the sweep does that.)
tests/_env_isolation_probe_*/
